docs/reviews\082-REVIEW-A.md:73:- [MINOR] docs/specs/parallel-wi-dispatch.md:100 -> §5.5/§8 assert "at most one owner per WI" and each lane completes "without occupying another WI", but §5.3 launches `agent_loop.py --track <lane>` "with the normal policy" and names no bound confining that lane loop to its single assignment — `agent_loop` on WI close rewrites the lane's `next-wi` to the next actionable and continues (agent_loop.py L2197-2201), so the property depends on an unspecified stop-after-assignment mechanism; a ratifiable design should state it -> name how the lane is confined to one WI (e.g. a single-WI/stop-at-close mode the dispatcher runs the lane under, or that the lane's self-advance yields control to the dispatcher rather than self-selecting a new WI) in §5 -> @owner
